  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Fair weather this weekend will give way to a \nreturn of rain Sunday night through Monday.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nHigh pressure continues through the day on Sunday, keeping dry\nweather and light winds in place. Temperatures remain mild, with\nhighs in the 70s across the forecast area. Clear skies tonight\ninto early Sunday morning will allow for efficient radiational\ncooling and could result in low temperatures dipping into the\nupper 40s across the north, and lower 50s Downeast.\n\nThe left exit region of an incoming jet streak aloft Sunday\nnight into Monday will support an incoming low pressure system,\nwith rain entering our area from the west after midnight Sunday\nnight. There is increasing consensus that a coastal low will\ndevelop along a front as it crosses the CWA, which could \nlocally enhance rainfall amounts Downeast. Rainfall totals may\napproach or even exceed an inch through the day on Monday,\nparticularly in areas of upslope flow such as the Central\nHighlands and into the Bangor region due to the development of\nthe coastal low.",
